u need to believe  in yourself it had definitely helped out  a lot and Perkins was there alongside  his brother and mother latisha Macias to  pin on his badge at graduation he hasn't  just been a mentor for him he's also  been a great dear friend that male  figure he was lacking at home I will  forever be grateful for that somewhere  along the line you guys came up with  nicknames yeah he would always tell me  I'm not here to replace your father  but I think he he was able to fill that  boy of that male figure that I didn't  have going up and I don't know where  when or where it started and started  calling him pops he calls you pops  you call him mijo Spanish for son  he's the son I never had in every sense  of the word today  Rodriguez patrols the streets of nearby  Placentia right now leading his own  police Explorer program came full circle  for me working with the kids and trying  to do my best I'm mentoring them and  using me you know the skills that I've  kind of grasped from Jason and trying to  do what he's done for me for all the  other kids there's so many lives out  there that he'll have an impact on in  his career my career is winding down but  his is just getting started  so that's that's why I say he'll do a  hundred times what I ever did in my  career he'll do in his there's a big  task sounds like he has a lot more  confidence than you like it than I do  but you'll be fine he'll be fine for CBS  this morning John Blackstone Garden  Grove California
 

